claim.claim-text:
1. A computer system for non-invasive computational biopsy for tissue classification and characterization, the system comprising:
a data synthesis module, and wherein the data synthesizer module is configured to receive images from a plurality of data sources and laboratory data from plurality of supplementary data sources, and wherein the data sources comprises at least one of X-ray scans, clinical images, and MRI images, and wherein the data synthesizer module is configured to process the received images for data synthesis, and the data synthesizer module is configured to create a multidimensional dataset (mdd), wherein multidimensional dataset is created by co-registering each voxel of the image with a vector of values, and the data synthesizer module is configured to create a mapped image by merging the multidimensional dataset with supplementary data sources;
an anomaly detector configured to create an anomaly score for each voxel of the merged dataset using an anomaly detection algorithms;
a Signal Filtering module, and wherein the Signal Filtering module is configured to receive the output from the anomaly detector for signal purification, wherein the Signal Filtering module generates filtered signals after signal purification;
a signal classification module, and wherein the signal classifier module is configured to compare the filtered signals with a database of pre-defined samples for classification, wherein the pre-defined samples are retrieved from a tissue definition database (TDD);
an Analysis Module, and wherein the Analysis Module is configured to analyze images based on multivariate statistics and machine learning to characterize tissues, wherein characterization enables visualization of tissue anomalies on a user interface; and a display module.

15. A computer implemented method comprising instructions stored on a non-transitory computer readable storage medium and executed on a hardware processor of a computing device comprising processors (e.g. CPUs and/or GPUs) and a memory, for non-invasive tissue classification and characterization, the method comprising:
receiving images from a plurality of data sources and a supplementary data sources, wherein the data sources comprises clinical images, CT Scan, MRI images, etc.;
processing the received images by a data synthesis/analysis module to create a set of observation vectors, and wherein the set of observation vectors include high level objects and low level objects;
creating a multidimensional dataset (mdd) by the data synthesis module, wherein multidimensional dataset is created by co-registering each voxel of the image with a vector of values;
creating a mapped image using the data synthesis module by merging the multidimensional dataset with supplementary data sources;
computing an anomaly score for each voxel of the merged dataset using anomaly detectors;
receiving an output from an anomaly detector by a Signal Filtering module for signal purification, wherein the Signal Filtering module is configured to generate filtered signals after signal purification;
comparing the filtered signals with a database of pre-defined samples for classification by a classifier module, wherein the pre-defined samples are retrieved from a tissue definition database (TDD); and
analyzing images based on multivariate statistics and machine learning techniques by the analysis module to characterize tissues, wherein the characterization is performed to display tissue anomalies on a user interface.
